#{[17592186296551 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{8}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296551 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296551 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0d9acb3-2434-56be-aa4c-a64c219f0e19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296674 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296674 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296674 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186296551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296674 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "12f4d372-a091-54bb-b1c9-2dc96c45bdc3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297271 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297271 #edb/ref 1069 "q-302240" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297271 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297271 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ for $x<0$ with $f(x)=\\frac{|8x-7|}{-5x+2}?$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote is $y=$\n\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297271 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9813cef-279a-5fd4-8e50-a7601280fe38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297271 #edb/ref 1074 "For large negative values of $x,$ we have $|8x-7|=-(8x-7).$ Consequently, for $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{|8x-7|}{-5x+2}={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8x-7)}{-5x+2}.\n$$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote for $x<0$ is $y={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8x-7)}{-5x+2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(\\frac{8x}{x}-\\frac{7}{x})}{(\\frac{-5x}{x}+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8-\\frac{7}{x})}{(-5+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(8-0)}{-5+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac{8}{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306214 #edb/ref 1080 "-p" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306214 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306214 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6f8fcbb2-96e8-57cf-8c64-d7dd950ff7b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308200 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186306214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308200 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308200 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308200 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186306214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308200 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d8eaeee4-55d9-5263-89e5-6270bb7aa9c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308610 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308610 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334383" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308610 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308610 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=p,$ express the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ in terms of $p.$\n\n${\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308610 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae73a5ce-ed7c-55ec-b81b-c25a686080d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308610 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x),$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x).$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)={e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & ={e}^{|-x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x) \\\\  & ={e}^{|x|}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)={e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x+p & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348777 #edb/ref 1080 "{q,s,u}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348777 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348777 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "267d9d8b-1274-53d3-8a4b-c06112646a6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348935 #edb/ref 1080 "{m,r,u}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348935 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348935 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "363ea4e8-13dc-54b5-bfbb-809cdabdec08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349163 #edb/ref 1080 "{p,r,u}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349163 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349163 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4f3f4c35-5e0c-5941-90ec-046ad29aa28c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349651 #edb/ref 1080 "{q,s,t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349651 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349651 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "83965187-1c9e-5eb9-af05-4ab85d838585" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349803 #edb/ref 1080 "{p,q,r,s,t,u}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349803 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349803 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "971d86f7-dd14-55b9-a3ae-4e0577582fab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351123 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351123 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348